    <string name="help_subtitle">Frequently asked questions</string>
    <string name="faq_scan_q">How do I scan a QR code or barcode?</string>
    <string name="faq_scan_a">Open the Scan tab and point your camera at the code inside the frame. It will be detected and decoded automatically.</string>
    <string name="faq_create_q">How do I create my own QR code?</string>
    <string name="faq_create_a">Go to the Create tab, choose a type (Text, URL, WiFi, Contact, etc.), fill in the details, and tap Create.</string>
    <string name="faq_customize_q">Can I customize the look of my QR code?</string>
    <string name="faq_customize_a">Yes. After creating a QR code, tap Continue Edit to change colors, pixel/corner/ball shapes, add a logo, or apply a ready-made template.</string>
    <string name="faq_gallery_q">Can I scan a QR code from a photo instead of the camera?</string>
    <string name="faq_gallery_a">Yes. On the Scan screen, tap the Gallery button and pick a photo that contains a QR code or barcode.</string>
    <string name="faq_history_q">Where can I find my past scans and created codes?</string>
    <string name="faq_history_a">Every scan and creation is saved automatically in the History tab, grouped by Today, Yesterday, This Week, and Older.</string>
    <string name="faq_favorite_q">How do I save a QR code as a favorite?</string>
    <string name="faq_favorite_a">Tap the star icon on any item in History, or on its result screen, to add it to Favorites for quick access later.</string>
    <string name="faq_permission_q">Why does the app need camera permission?</string>
    <string name="faq_permission_a">Camera access is required to scan QR codes and barcodes. The app does not use the camera for anything else.</string>
